# cp .env.example .env  and fill in the key for the backend you use.
#
# Read from the repository root by utils/env.py, which entry points call
# explicitly -- nothing in utils/ touches os.environ on import. A shell variable
# wins over this file, so a one-off
#
#     GEMINI_API_KEY=... python scripts/vlm_probe.py ...
#
# overrides whatever is set here. .env is gitignored; this file is not, so it
# must never hold a real key.

# --- gemini (default backend) ------------------------------------------------
# Either name works; GEMINI_API_KEY is checked first.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Note on quota: image-bearing requests draw on a different budget from
# text-only ones. A key that answers a text prompt fine can still refuse a
# request carrying a single image with 429, so testing a key with a text call
# tells you nothing about whether an experiment can run.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- claude (--backend claude) -----------------------------------------------
# Optional. The Anthropic SDK also picks up an `ant auth login` profile, so a
# missing variable here is not conclusive and utils/env.py lets the SDK decide.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
